followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkeyzuwu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkeyzuwu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkeyzuwu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkeyzuwu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkeyzuwu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkeyzuwu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkeyzuwu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkeyzuwu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-09T15:32:28Z","updated_at":"2025-11-09T15:33:35Z","body":"I have managed to fix the initial \"bug\" with saving the class name of the variable in the `DraggedExport` struct and checking it against the property type hint.\r\n\r\nWhile this does work, like you said it seems to be a separate problem. If you also change the type of the `@export` variable, it does not reset the value and keeps it assigned. Fixing this would have to be done in a separate PR since it doesn't have to do with drag-n-drop export variables, its just how export variables work in general.\r\n\r\nThere is an issue and PR about it: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104323, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104338\r\nThe change was introduced here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/84446\r\n\r\nAnyways, updated to fix the original bug that this exposes with the name collision. Changing the type _while_ the name collision error is happening does work correctly so I think it's fine. Don't like how it adds yet another for loop where if its a giant class it will run through a lot of properties, but I don't see a work around. It does only run once when the script doesn't have errors anymore though, so I think its fine.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/c